  Well, I can't speak for everyone else, but I had started to write
something, but then I decided I was confused about what you were
asking because your use of English was very confusing.  But I think
what you are suggesting is that you would like a structure like "mi
fijoibai do jmive zei lifri" to mean the same thing as "mi fi do bai
do jmive ze lifri"?  (Incidentally, even within FA itself, I always
wondered why we couldn't do "mi tavla fi ja fo la lojban" ("we talk
about and in lojban".)  Not sure I'd be willing to mixing modals and
FA, but on the other hand, why not?)  If that's what you meant, then
yeah, I always thought it would be useful, and it does have analogues
in natlangs, as I've shown)

